Raising this as part of GSSoC 2026.

### Description

In `app/api/streak/route.ts`, when both `org` and `versus` query parameters are provided, the `versus` calendar is never fetched:

if (org) {
  const orgData = await getOrgDashboardData(org, { ... });
  calendar = orgData.calendar;
  // versus is never fetched here
} else {
  // versus is only fetched in this branch
  if (versus) { ... }
}

Since `versusCalendar` remains `undefined`, the condition `else if (versus && versusCalendar)` is never true and the response silently falls through to the default single-user SVG with no error.


### Steps to Reproduce

1. Request /api/streak?user=someorg&org=someorg&versus=otheruser
2. Observe a normal single-user badge is returned, not a versus badge
3. No error is returned — versus param is silently dropped

### Expected Behavior

The versus calendar should be fetched alongside org data, or a 400 error returned indicating org and versus cannot be combined.

### Screenshots / Logs

N/A

### GitHub Username (If applicable)

N/A

### Environment

Chrome

### Description

In `app/api/streak/route.ts`, when both `org` and `versus` query parameters are provided, the `versus` calendar is never fetched:

if (org) {
  const orgData = await getOrgDashboardData(org, { ... });
  calendar = orgData.calendar;
  // versus is never fetched here
} else {
  // versus is only fetched in this branch
  if (versus) {
    const versusData = await fetchGitHubContributions(versus, { ... });
    versusCalendar = versusData.calendar;
  }
}

Since `versusCalendar` remains `undefined`, the condition `else if (versus && versusCalendar)` is never true, and the response silently falls through to the default single-user SVG with no error message or indication that the `versus` param was ignored.

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Make a request to /api/streak?user=someorg&org=someorg&versus=otheruser
2. Observe the response is a normal single-user badge, not a versus badge
3. No error is returned — the versus param is silently dropped

### Expected Behavior

Either the versus calendar should be fetched alongside the org data, or a clear 400 error should be returned indicating that org and versus cannot be used together.

